  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hi, how have you been?",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_05"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Good, thanks. Just got home.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 0.85,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_19"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "How do people read fifty books a year? I barely manage five.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.34,
   "block": "books.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Mostly small habits. Twenty minutes before bed, a book always in your bag, and audiobooks during chores add up fast.",
   "est_sec": 6.3,
   "gap_before": 0.42,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I always fall asleep reading in bed though.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 2.81,
   "block": "books.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then try reading in the morning with your coffee, or at lunch. Some people find that sticks better.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.35,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Is it okay to quit a book halfway if I'm not enjoying it?",
   "est_sec": 4.13,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "books.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Definitely. Life's too short. Dropping a dull book is one of the best ways to read more.",
   "est_sec": 5.37,
   "gap_before": 0.6,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "That makes me feel better. I've been stuck on the same one",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.8,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "books.dlg2"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "since July, honestly.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.92,
   "block": "books.dlg2",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
